'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  test-divide-by-zero.spin2
''   Purpose....  Measure what the P2 returns when it divides by zero: the
''                CORDIC QDIV and QFRAC (with and without SETQ), and the
''                Spin2 operators /, //, +/, +// and MULDIV64
''   Manual.....  P2 Knowledge Base
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Oct 2026
''   Updated....  Oct 2026
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ WHAT IS MEASURED

  No source states what a divide by zero returns.  The P2 silicon
  documentation (CORDIC Solver, DIVIDE) gives QDIV {Q:D}/S and QFRAC {D:Q}/S
  with the quotient in GETQX and the remainder in GETQY, and says nothing of
  S = 0.  The Spin2 language documentation lists /, //, +/, +//, FRAC,
  their assignment forms /=, //=, +/=, +//=, and MULDIV64 (unsigned), and
  says nothing of a zero divisor either.

  This program MEASURES the results; it predicts no value.  What it proves:
    - the CORDIC path and the read-out are sound: controls with non-zero
      divisors MUST give their exact results, or RIG FAIL;
    - each zero-divisor result is a result of THAT operation, not a stale
      one: before every repetition a MARKER divide with a different, known
      result runs (checked exact), so a GETQX that returned the previous
      result would show the marker's value and differ between repetitions;
    - determinism: every case runs 8 times; DETERMINISTIC = all 8 identical,
      VARIES = not (every repetition is printed raw);
    - whether a zero-divisor operation leaves the CORDIC in a bad state: the
      NEXT divide after it (1000 / 3) is checked, and its count printed;
    - the clocks from GETCT before the operation to GETCT after its GETQX,
      for zero-divisor cases beside the controls that run the same code.

THE SPIN2 OPERATORS, FROM THE SPIN2 INTERPRETER SOURCE
  The compiler emits one bytecode per operator; the interpreter runs it as
  a skip pattern over shared code (mul_mod / muu_mod).  None tests the
  divisor for zero; each passes it to QDIV or QFRAC as a register:
    a / b    bc_div   ($97): w := |b| (C = sign of b); x := a; Z = sign of
             a; x := |a|; QDIV x,w; x := GETQX; negate x if C <> Z
    a // b   bc_rem   ($99): as /, but x := GETQY; negate x if a < 0
    a +/ b   bc_divu  ($98): QDIV a,b; GETQX
    a +// b  bc_remu  ($9A): QDIV a,b; GETQY
    a FRAC b bc_frac  ($9D): QFRAC a,b; GETQX     ({a:0} / b)
    a /= b, a //= b, a +/= b, a +//= b: bc_div_write, bc_rem_write,
             bc_divu_write, bc_remu_write ($4C, $4E, $4D, $4F): the same
             code as the operator, then the result written back to a
    MULDIV64(m1,m2,d)  bc_muldiv64 ($92), muldiv64_: QMUL m1,m2 -> {hi,lo};
             then SKIP into the GETSEC code: SETQ hi; QDIV lo,d; GETQX
  So a Spin2 divide by zero is QDIV |a|,0 (or {hi:lo}/0, or QFRAC a,0)
  plus, for the signed operators, the sign step above.  The controls below
  include negative operands so the sign step is proven on the part.

RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz.  No pins, no jumpers, no instruments.
  Cog 0 (Spin2, the only cog with the debugger) starts the measuring cog,
  waits for it (1 s timeout), checks and prints its records; then starts a
  Spin2 cog for the Spin2 cases, waits (1 s timeout), checks and prints.
  The measuring cog (COGINIT, cog execution, PASM below) has no debug
  interrupt, no debug() and no BRK, and sets up no interrupt; the Spin2
  cog calls no debug().

ONE PASM RUN (case c, repetition r; measuring cog)
    MARKER   qdiv c_mkd,c_mks: c_mkd = 7 * m + k, c_mks = 7, m = $0010_0000
             + c * 16 + r, k = (r & 3) + 1; GETQX / GETQY (MUST be m, k)
    CASE     getct t0 / [setq Q] / qdiv-or-qfrac D,S / getqx QX / getct t1 /
             getqy QY  (one hand-written copy per form, below)
    NEXT     qdiv c_fud,c_fus (1000 / 3); GETQX / GETQY (333 and 1 if the
             CORDIC is sound after the case)
    record   marker QX, marker QY, QX, QY, t1 - t0, next QX, next QY, tag
             (tag = $7A90_0000 + c * 16 + r, written in the same block, so a
             record never written shows a wrong tag)

PASM CASES (P00..P60; the table pcaseTbl below)
  CONTROLS (P00..P10), each MUST give exactly, in all 8 repetitions.  Every
  form that has a zero-divisor case below has a control here:
    P00 qdiv D,S          1000 / 3                 QX 333          QY 1
    P01 qdiv D,S          $FFFF_FFFF / 2           QX $7FFF_FFFF   QY 1
    P02 qdiv D,S          0 / 5                    QX 0            QY 0
    P03 qdiv D,S          7 / $FFFF_FFFF           QX 0            QY 7
    P04 qdiv D,#7         $1234_5678 / 7           QX $0299_C335   QY 5
    P05 setq Q/qdiv D,S   {$1234_5678:$9ABC_DEF0} / $8765_4321
                                                   QX $226B_9022   QY $38BC_648E
    P06 qfrac D,S         {1:0} / 3                QX $5555_5555   QY 1
    P07 setq Q/qfrac D,S  {1:$8000_0000} / 7       QX $36DB_6DB6   QY 6
    P08 qfrac D,#7        {1:0} / 7                QX $2492_4924   QY 4
    P09 setq Q/qdiv D,#7  {3:$1234_5678} / 7       QX $7050_9EA3   QY 3
    P10 setq Q/qfrac D,#7 {2:$1234_5678} / 7       QX $4BBE_557E   QY 6
  The #7 forms run the same copies as the #0 forms except for the S field:
  a control on #7 proves the immediate path of each form.
  ZERO DIVISOR (P11..P60), each measured (QX, QY, clocks):
    P11..P24  qdiv D,#0 and qdiv D,S (S = 0), D = 0, 1, 7, $7FFF_FFFF,
              $8000_0000, $FFFF_FFFF, $1234_5678 (each D: #0 form, then S)
    P25..P36  setq Q / qdiv D,S (S = 0), Q = 1, $FFFF_FFFF, $1234_5678,
              D = 0, 7, $FFFF_FFFF; and setq Q / qdiv D,#0 with D = 7
    P37..P48  qfrac D,#0 and qfrac D,S (S = 0), D = 0, 1, 7, $8000_0000,
              $FFFF_FFFF, $1234_5678
    P49..P60  setq Q / qfrac D,S (S = 0), Q = 1, $FFFF_FFFF, $1234_5678,
              D = 0, 1, $1234_5678; and setq Q / qfrac D,#0 with D = 1

SPIN2 CASES (S00..S70; the table scaseTbl below), run in a Spin2 cog by one
  method for every case, with every operand a parameter, so the compiler
  cannot fold the divisor.  Before every repetition a MARKER divide
  (7 * m + k) +/ 7 (MUST be m); after it a NEXT divide 1000 +/ 3.
  CONTROLS (S00..S20), each MUST give exactly, in all 8 repetitions:
    1000 / 3 = 333   -1000 / 3 = -333   1000 / -3 = -333   -1000 / -3 = 333
    1000 // 3 = 1    -1000 // 3 = -1    1000 // -3 = 1     -1000 // -3 = -1
    $FFFF_FFFF +/ 2 = $7FFF_FFFF        1000 +/ 3 = 333
    $FFFF_FFFF +// 2 = 1                1000 +// 7 = 6
    MULDIV64(1000, 1000, 3) = 333333
    MULDIV64($FFFF_FFFF, $FFFF_FFFF, $FFFF_FFFF) = $FFFF_FFFF
    MULDIV64($1234_5678, $10, 3) = $6117_2280
    1 FRAC 3 = $5555_5555               2 FRAC 7 = $4924_9249
    a := -1000, a /= 3: -333            a := -1000, a //= 3: -1
    a := $FFFF_FFFF, a +/= 2: $7FFF_FFFF
    a := 1000, a +//= 7: 6
  ZERO DIVISOR (S21..S70), each measured:
    a / 0 and a // 0, a = 0, 1, 7, -1, -7, $7FFF_FFFF, NEGX, $1234_5678,
      -$1234_5678
    a +/ 0 and a +// 0, a = 0, 1, 7, $7FFF_FFFF, $8000_0000, $FFFF_FFFF,
      $1234_5678
    MULDIV64(m1, m2, 0), (m1, m2) = (0, 0), (0, 12345), (1, 1), (7, 3),
      (1000, 1000), ($1234_5678, $10), ($FFFF_FFFF, $FFFF_FFFF),
      ($1234_5678, $9ABC_DEF0)
    a FRAC 0, a = 0, 1, 7, $8000_0000, $FFFF_FFFF, $1234_5678
    a /= 0 and a //= 0 with a = -7; a +/= 0 and a +//= 0 with
      a = $FFFF_FFFF (each also measured above in its operator form)

CHECKS (each failure prints RIG FAIL)
  Before the runs: the case tables hold the counts the program declares,
    and every row names a known form or operator.
  Measuring cog and Spin2 cog: started, and done within 1 s.  If not, the
    cases before the one the cog stopped in are reported, then a STALLED
    line names that case and repetition and the next line prints its
    repetitions that did complete; a cog that never reported a run is
    named as such.  The END line says STALLED.
  Every PASM record: its tag right; its marker right.
  Every control: its value right in all 8 repetitions, and its NEXT divide
    right in all 8.
  Every Spin2 marker right.
  A zero-divisor case is never a RIG FAIL: its values, its agreement, how
    often it equals the marker before it, and its NEXT count are measured
    and printed.

OUTPUT, PER CASE (two lines)
  P..: the form and operands; repetition 0's QX and QY in hex and unsigned
       decimal; DETERMINISTIC (8 of 8 identical) or VARIES (n of 8 identical
       to repetition 0); "equal to the marker before it" n of 8; "next
       divide right" n of 8; clocks min..max; controls add CONTROL OK or
       CONTROL MISS with the expected values.
  raw: every repetition's QX, QY and clocks.
  S..: the operator and operands (hex and decimal); repetition 0's result;
       DETERMINISTIC or VARIES; "equal to the marker before it" n of 8 (the
       marker's quotient m for /, +/, FRAC, MULDIV64 and their assignment
       forms, its remainder k for //, +// and theirs; either sign for the
       signed operators); "next divide right"; controls CONTROL OK or
       CONTROL MISS.  raw: every repetition's result.
  A VARIES case whose "equal to the marker" count is not 0 is returning
  stale results; one whose count is 0 really varies.  (MULDIV64 runs its
  own QMUL between the marker and its QDIV, so for MULDIV64 the count
  tests the marker only, not that QMUL's product.)
  Then SUMMARY lines, a CONTROLS line, and the END line.

OPCODES (pnut-ts -d -l, v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, read from the .lst hub
  image; object offset = cog address * 4 + $BF0).  QDIV is 1101000 1LI,
  QFRAC 1101001 0LI; I = 1: S is the 9-bit immediate.  Cog registers: c_mks
  $08D, c_fud $08E, c_fus $08F, dval $092, sval $093, qval $094, c_rp $096,
  c_vec $09B, c_mkd $09D, c_t0 $09F, c_t1 $0A0, record block r_mkx..r_tag
  $0A1..$0A8 (r_qx $0A3, r_qy $0A4).
  Every form is, in order: getct c_t0 ($FD613E1A) / [setq qval
  ($FD612828)] / the operation / getqx r_qx ($FD614618) / getct c_t1
  ($FD61401A) / getqy r_qy ($FD614819) / jmp #case_done.  Each form's
  label address, then its operation (the second long, or the third after
  a SETQ):
    f_div_imm0    $CB8  qdiv dval,#0     $FD152400  I=1, S=#0
    f_div_reg     $CD0  qdiv dval,sval   $FD112493  I=0, S=$093
    f_divq_imm0   $CE8  qdiv dval,#0     $FD152400  after the SETQ
    f_divq_reg    $D04  qdiv dval,sval   $FD112493  after the SETQ
    f_frac_imm0   $D20  qfrac dval,#0    $FD252400  I=1, S=#0
    f_frac_reg    $D38  qfrac dval,sval  $FD212493  I=0, S=$093
    f_fracq_imm0  $D50  qfrac dval,#0    $FD252400  after the SETQ
    f_fracq_reg   $D6C  qfrac dval,sval  $FD212493  after the SETQ
    f_div_immk    $D88  qdiv dval,#7     $FD152407  I=1, S=#7 (P04)
    f_frac_immk   $DA0  qfrac dval,#7    $FD252407  I=1, S=#7 (P08)
    f_divq_immk   $DB8  qdiv dval,#7     $FD152407  after the SETQ (P09)
    f_fracq_immk  $DD4  qfrac dval,#7    $FD252407  after the SETQ (P10)
    qdiv c_mkd,c_mks   $FD113A8D  the MARKER ($C60), then getqx r_mkx /
                                  getqy r_mky / jmp c_vec ($FD61362C)
    qdiv c_fud,c_fus   $FD111C8F  the NEXT divide ($C78)
    setq #7 / wrlong r_mkx,c_rp  $FD640E28 / $FC614296  the 8-long record
    kvec_tab ($DF0)    $032 $038 $03E $045 $04C $052 $058 $05F $066 $06C
                       $072 $079: the cog addresses of the twelve forms,
                       in K_* order
  The one Spin2 method that runs every Spin2 case (object offset $268A):
    E1 E2 97 F4 (a / b), E1 E2 99 F4 (//), E1 E2 98 F4 (+/), E1 E2 9A F4
    (+//), E1 E2 E3 19 92 F4 (MULDIV64), E1 E2 9D F4 (FRAC), and for the
    assignment forms E1 F4 (result := a) then E2 D4 4C (/=), E2 D4 4E
    (//=), E2 D4 4D (+/=), E2 D4 4F (+//=): every divisor is a local read
    at run time (E2, or E3 for MULDIV64), so none is folded at compile
    time.
  If you edit this file, recompile with -l and re-read every row above.

DEBUG OUTPUT.  Every printed line is assembled in lineBuf from hub strings
  and numbers and sent by the ONE debug(zstr_(@lineBuf)) record in ln_out();
  the only other record is debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION").  The listing reports
  2 DEBUG records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.

HOW TO RUN
  Compile with pnut-ts -d, load to RAM with DEBUG on (pnut-term-ts, or PNut
  Ctrl-F10).  Runs once, in well under a second; nothing written to flash.
  Output: the header, two lines per case (61 PASM, 71 Spin2), the SUMMARY
  and CONTROLS lines, the END line, then DEBUG_END_SESSION.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000         ' system clock: 200 MHz
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001          ' debug interrupt in cog 0 ONLY

  REPS            = 8                   ' repetitions of every case
  NPCASE          = 61                  ' PASM cases (pcaseTbl rows)
  NPCTRL          = 11                  ' PASM controls: the first rows
  NSCASE          = 71                  ' Spin2 cases (scaseTbl rows)
  NSCTRL          = 21                  ' Spin2 controls: the first rows
  CASE_W          = 6                   ' longs per pcaseTbl row
  SCASE_W         = 5                   ' longs per scaseTbl row
  RECW            = 8                   ' longs per PASM record

  MK_BASE         = $0010_0000          ' marker quotient m = MK_BASE + case * 16 + rep
  MK_CASE_SHIFT   = 4                   ' case * 16 (REPS <= 16)
  MK_S            = 7                   ' marker divisor
  MK_REM_MASK     = 3                   ' marker remainder k = (rep & 3) + 1
  FU_D            = 1000                ' NEXT divide: 1000 / 3
  FU_S            = 3
  FU_QX           = 333
  FU_QY           = 1
  CTL_IMM_S       = 7                   ' P04, P08..P10: the #7 controls
  TAG_BASE        = $7A90_0000          ' record tag = TAG_BASE + case * 16 + rep
  DONE_V          = $0D0E_0D0E          ' a cog is done
  UNWRITTEN       = $EEEE_EEEE          ' record fill before a run
  CUR_REP_MASK    = $F                  ' progress long: case * 16 + rep

  SPIN_STACK      = 128                 ' longs of stack for the Spin2 cog
  LINE_MAX        = 480                 ' longest printed line (chars)
  DEC_TOP         = 1_000_000_000       ' top decimal place of a long
  DEC_DIGITS      = 10
  DEC_BASE        = 10
  HEX_DIGITS      = 8
  HEX_BITS        = 4
  HEX_GROUP       = 4                   ' "_" after the top four hex digits
  HEX_LETTERS     = 10                  ' nibbles 10..15 print as A..F
  NGRP            = 4                   ' clock groups (G_*)

CON ' ---- Identifiers ----
  ' PASM forms (kvec_tab order in the measuring cog)
  #0, K_DIV_IMM0, K_DIV_REG, K_DIVQ_IMM0, K_DIVQ_REG, K_FRAC_IMM0, K_FRAC_REG, K_FRACQ_IMM0, K_FRACQ_REG
  #K_FRACQ_REG + 1, K_DIV_IMMK, K_FRAC_IMMK, K_DIVQ_IMMK, K_FRACQ_IMMK  ' the #7 forms
  NKIND           = K_FRACQ_IMMK + 1

  ' pcaseTbl row longs: form, D, S, Q, expected QX, expected QY (controls)
  #0, CW_KIND, CW_D, CW_S, CW_Q, CW_EXPX, CW_EXPY

  ' PASM record longs
  #0, RW_MKX, RW_MKY, RW_QX, RW_QY, RW_CLK, RW_FUX, RW_FUY, RW_TAG

  ' Spin2 operators: the operator forms, then the assignment forms
  '  (OP_DIVA /=, OP_REMA //=, OP_DIVUA +/=, OP_REMUA +//=)
  #0, OP_DIV, OP_REM, OP_DIVU, OP_REMU, OP_MD64, OP_FRAC, OP_DIVA, OP_REMA, OP_DIVUA, OP_REMUA
  NOP_KIND        = OP_REMUA + 1

  ' scaseTbl row longs: operator, a, b, c (MULDIV64 divisor), expected (controls)
  #0, SW_OP, SW_A, SW_B, SW_C, SW_EXP

  ' clock groups: controls / zero-divisor cases, without / with SETQ
  #0, G_CTRL_PLAIN, G_CTRL_SETQ, G_ZERO_PLAIN, G_ZERO_SETQ

  ' mailbox longs (cog 0 <-> measuring cog)
  '  MB_TBL   - hub address of pcaseTbl
  '  MB_REC   - hub address of the records
  '  MB_NCASE - number of cases to run
  '  MB_CUR   - progress: case * 16 + rep of the run about to start
  '  MB_DONE  - DONE_V once every case has run
  #0, MB_TBL, MB_REC, MB_NCASE, MB_CUR, MB_DONE, MB_LEN

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long mbox[MB_LEN]
  long precs[NPCASE * REPS * RECW]      ' PASM records
  long spinRes[NSCASE * REPS]           ' Spin2: the case's result
  long spinMk[NSCASE * REPS]            ' Spin2: the marker's result
  long spinFu[NSCASE * REPS]            ' Spin2: the NEXT divide's result
  long spinCur                          ' Spin2 progress: case * 16 + rep
  long spinDone                         ' DONE_V once every Spin2 case has run
  long spinStack[SPIN_STACK]
  long failCnt                          ' RIG FAIL lines printed
  long pRanCnt, sRanCnt                 ' cases fully run (PASM, Spin2)
  long bPasmStall, bSpinStall           ' a cog did not finish within 1 s
  long pDetCnt, pVarCnt                 ' PASM zero cases DETERMINISTIC / VARIES
  long pEqMkCnt, pNextCnt, pRunCnt      ' PASM zero runs: equal to marker, next right, all
  long sDetCnt, sVarCnt                 ' Spin2 zero cases DETERMINISTIC / VARIES
  long sEqMkCnt, sNextCnt, sRunCnt      ' Spin2 zero runs: equal to marker, next right, all
  long grpLo[NGRP], grpHi[NGRP]         ' clock range per G_* group
  ' every printed line is built here and sent by ONE debug() record (ln_out)
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos

PUB main() | pasmCog, spinCog, caseIdx
'' Run the PASM cases on the measuring cog and the Spin2 cases on a Spin2
'' cog, print every case, the controls, the summary and the END line.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local pasmCog - cog the measuring cog started in
' @local spinCog - cog the Spin2 cases ran in
' @local caseIdx - case index

  linePos := 0
  failCnt := 0
  reset_tallies()
  print_header()
  if not tables_ok()
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL (case tables) ==="))
    finish()

  ' ---- PASM cases ----
  longfill(@precs, UNWRITTEN, NPCASE * REPS * RECW)
  mbox[MB_TBL] := @pcaseTbl
  mbox[MB_REC] := @precs
  mbox[MB_NCASE] := NPCASE
  mbox[MB_CUR] := UNWRITTEN
  mbox[MB_DONE] := 0
  pasmCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @pasm, @mbox)
  if pasmCog < 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: coginit expected a free cog (0..7), got "))
    ln_d(pasmCog)
    ln_out()
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL (no measuring cog) ==="))
    finish()
  pRanCnt := NPCASE
  if not wait_done(@mbox[MB_DONE])
    bPasmStall := TRUE
    cogstop(pasmCog)
    pRanCnt := ran_count(mbox[MB_CUR], NPCASE)
  ln_s(string("=== PASM: measuring cog "))
  ln_d(pasmCog)
  say(string(" ==="))
  if pRanCnt > 0
    repeat caseIdx from 0 to pRanCnt - 1
      report_pcase(caseIdx)
  if bPasmStall
    print_pstall(mbox[MB_CUR])

  ' ---- Spin2 cases ----
  longfill(@spinRes, UNWRITTEN, NSCASE * REPS)
  longfill(@spinMk, UNWRITTEN, NSCASE * REPS)
  longfill(@spinFu, UNWRITTEN, NSCASE * REPS)
  spinCur := UNWRITTEN
  spinDone := 0
  spinCog := cogspin(NEWCOG, spin_worker(), @spinStack)
  if spinCog < 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: cogspin expected a free cog (0..7), got "))
    ln_d(spinCog)
    ln_out()
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL (no Spin2 cog) ==="))
    finish()
  sRanCnt := NSCASE
  if not wait_done(@spinDone)
    bSpinStall := TRUE
    cogstop(spinCog)
    sRanCnt := ran_count(spinCur, NSCASE)
  ln_s(string("=== SPIN2: Spin2 cog "))
  ln_d(spinCog)
  say(string(" ==="))
  if sRanCnt > 0
    repeat caseIdx from 0 to sRanCnt - 1
      report_scase(caseIdx)
  if bSpinStall
    print_sstall(spinCur)

  print_summary()
  finish()

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when END_SESSION or
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_u(numVal) | divisor, digitVal, bStarted
' Append an unsigned decimal (the form udec_ printed) to the line; the
' number is read as unsigned.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local digitVal - the digit at that place
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  divisor := DEC_TOP
  bStarted := FALSE
  repeat DEC_DIGITS
    digitVal := numVal +/ divisor
    if digitVal <> 0 or bStarted or divisor == 1
      ln_c("0" + digitVal)
      bStarted := TRUE
    numVal := numVal +// divisor
    divisor /= DEC_BASE

PRI ln_d(numVal)
' Append a signed decimal (the form sdec_ printed) to the line; the number
' is read as signed.
'
' @param numVal - the number

  if numVal < 0
    ln_c("-")
    ln_u(-numVal)
  else
    ln_u(numVal)

PRI ln_h(numVal) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as uhex_long_ printed it: $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from HEX_DIGITS - 1 to 0
    nibble := (numVal >> (idx * HEX_BITS)) & $F
    if nibble < HEX_LETTERS
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - HEX_LETTERS)
    if idx == HEX_GROUP
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_hu(numVal)
' Append "$XXXX_XXXX (unsigned decimal)".
'
' @param numVal - the number

  ln_h(numVal)
  ln_s(string(" ("))
  ln_u(numVal)
  ln_c(")")

PRI ln_hs(numVal)
' Append "$XXXX_XXXX (signed decimal)".
'
' @param numVal - the number

  ln_h(numVal)
  ln_s(string(" ("))
  ln_d(numVal)
  ln_c(")")

PRI ln_cnt(countVal)
' Append "n of 8".
'
' @param countVal - the count

  ln_d(countVal)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(REPS)

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

PRI rig_fail(pStr)
' Count one RIG FAIL and start its line: "RIG FAIL: " and the string.  The
' caller appends the details and sends the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  failCnt++
  ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
  ln_s(pStr)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' set-up
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_header()
' Print the rig identity, the record layout, every control's MUST value and
' how each case is described, before any run.
'

  say(string("=== Divide by zero: CORDIC QDIV / QFRAC and the Spin2 divide operators (pnut-ts v1.55.8 -d, clk 200 MHz) ==="))
  say(string("Measured, not predicted: every zero-divisor value is printed. Controls with non-zero divisors MUST be exact, else RIG FAIL."))
  say(string("PASM run (case c, rep r): MARKER qdiv (7*m+k)/7, m = $0010_0000 + c*16 + r, k = (r & 3) + 1, MUST give m, k | CASE getct / [setq Q] / qdiv-or-qfrac D,S / getqx QX / getct / getqy QY | NEXT qdiv 1000/3"))
  say(string("PASM controls MUST (all 8 reps, and NEXT 333 r 1): P00 1000/3 = 333 r 1 | P01 $FFFF_FFFF/2 = $7FFF_FFFF r 1 | P02 0/5 = 0 r 0 | P03 7/$FFFF_FFFF = 0 r 7 | P04 $1234_5678/#7 = $0299_C335 r 5"))
  say(string("  P05 setq $1234_5678 qdiv $9ABC_DEF0/$8765_4321 = $226B_9022 r $38BC_648E | P06 qfrac 1/3 = $5555_5555 r 1 | P07 setq $8000_0000 qfrac 1/7 = $36DB_6DB6 r 6"))
  say(string("  P08 qfrac 1/#7 = $2492_4924 r 4 | P09 setq 3 qdiv $1234_5678/#7 = $7050_9EA3 r 3 | P10 setq $1234_5678 qfrac 2/#7 = $4BBE_557E r 6"))
  say(string("Spin2 run: MARKER (7*m+k) +/ 7 MUST give m | CASE the operator on a and b (MULDIV64: a, b, c), every operand a run-time parameter | NEXT 1000 +/ 3"))
  say(string("Spin2 controls MUST (all 8 reps): 1000/3 = 333, -1000/3 = -333, 1000/-3 = -333, -1000/-3 = 333, 1000//3 = 1, -1000//3 = -1, 1000//-3 = 1, -1000//-3 = -1,"))
  say(string("  $FFFF_FFFF +/ 2 = $7FFF_FFFF, 1000 +/ 3 = 333, $FFFF_FFFF +// 2 = 1, 1000 +// 7 = 6, MULDIV64(1000,1000,3) = 333333, MULDIV64($FFFF_FFFF,$FFFF_FFFF,$FFFF_FFFF) = $FFFF_FFFF, MULDIV64($1234_5678,$10,3) = $6117_2280,"))
  say(string("  1 FRAC 3 = $5555_5555, 2 FRAC 7 = $4924_9249, a := -1000 a /= 3 = -333, a := -1000 a //= 3 = -1, a := $FFFF_FFFF a +/= 2 = $7FFF_FFFF, a := 1000 a +//= 7 = 6"))
  say(string("Per case: rep 0's values; DETERMINISTIC = all 8 reps identical, VARIES = not; equal to the marker before it n of 8 (not 0 = stale results); next divide right n of 8; PASM clocks = GETCT before the op to GETCT after its GETQX (min..max)"))

PRI tables_ok() : bOk | caseIdx
' Check that the case tables hold the declared counts and only known forms
' and operators; print RIG FAIL for each that does not.
'
' @returns bOk - TRUE when both tables are as declared

' Local Variables:
' @local caseIdx - case index

  bOk := TRUE
  if @pzeroTbl - @pcaseTbl <> NPCTRL * CASE_W * 4 or @pcaseEnd - @pcaseTbl <> NPCASE * CASE_W * 4
    rig_fail(string("pcaseTbl expected "))
    ln_d(NPCTRL)
    ln_s(string(" control rows of "))
    ln_d(NPCASE)
    ln_s(string(", holds "))
    ln_d((@pzeroTbl - @pcaseTbl) / (CASE_W * 4))
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d((@pcaseEnd - @pcaseTbl) / (CASE_W * 4))
    ln_out()
    bOk := FALSE
  if @szeroTbl - @scaseTbl <> NSCTRL * SCASE_W * 4 or @scaseEnd - @scaseTbl <> NSCASE * SCASE_W * 4
    rig_fail(string("scaseTbl expected "))
    ln_d(NSCTRL)
    ln_s(string(" control rows of "))
    ln_d(NSCASE)
    ln_s(string(", holds "))
    ln_d((@szeroTbl - @scaseTbl) / (SCASE_W * 4))
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d((@scaseEnd - @scaseTbl) / (SCASE_W * 4))
    ln_out()
    bOk := FALSE
  if bOk
    repeat caseIdx from 0 to NPCASE - 1
      if long[pcase_row(caseIdx)][CW_KIND] +>= NKIND
        rig_fail(string("pcaseTbl row "))
        ln_d(caseIdx)
        ln_s(string(" names form "))
        ln_d(long[pcase_row(caseIdx)][CW_KIND])
        ln_out()
        bOk := FALSE
    repeat caseIdx from 0 to NSCASE - 1
      if long[scase_row(caseIdx)][SW_OP] +>= NOP_KIND
        rig_fail(string("scaseTbl row "))
        ln_d(caseIdx)
        ln_s(string(" names operator "))
        ln_d(long[scase_row(caseIdx)][SW_OP])
        ln_out()
        bOk := FALSE

PRI reset_tallies()
' Clear every tally.
'

  pRanCnt := 0
  sRanCnt := 0
  bPasmStall := FALSE
  bSpinStall := FALSE
  pDetCnt := 0
  pVarCnt := 0
  pEqMkCnt := 0
  pNextCnt := 0
  pRunCnt := 0
  sDetCnt := 0
  sVarCnt := 0
  sEqMkCnt := 0
  sNextCnt := 0
  sRunCnt := 0
  longfill(@grpLo, POSX, NGRP)
  longfill(@grpHi, NEGX, NGRP)

PRI wait_done(pFlag) : bDone | startCt
' Wait up to 1 s for a cog to write DONE_V to its done long.
'
' @param pFlag - hub address of the done long
' @returns bDone - TRUE when DONE_V arrived in time

' Local Variables:
' @local startCt - CT when the wait began

  bDone := TRUE
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until long[pFlag] == DONE_V
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      bDone := FALSE
      quit

PRI ran_count(progressVal, caseCnt) : ranCnt
' The cases fully run before a cog stalled, from its progress long.
'
' @param progressVal - the progress long: case * 16 + rep, or UNWRITTEN
'   if the cog never started a run
' @param caseCnt - the cases in the cog's table
' @returns ranCnt - cases before the one the cog stopped in (0..caseCnt)

  if progressVal == UNWRITTEN
    ranCnt := 0
  else
    ranCnt := (progressVal >> MK_CASE_SHIFT) <# caseCnt

PRI ln_stall(pWho, prefixChar, progressVal)
' Send the STALLED line of a cog: never reported, or the case and the
' repetition it stopped in.
'
' @param pWho - hub address of the cog's name, as printed
' @param prefixChar - "P" or "S"
' @param progressVal - the progress long: case * 16 + rep, or UNWRITTEN
'   if the cog never started a run

  ln_s(string("STALLED: the "))
  ln_s(pWho)
  if progressVal == UNWRITTEN
    say(string(" never reported - it started no run within 1 s"))
  else
    ln_s(string(" did not finish within 1 s; it stopped in case "))
    ln_case(prefixChar, progressVal >> MK_CASE_SHIFT)
    ln_s(string("repetition "))
    ln_d(progressVal & CUR_REP_MASK)
    ln_s(string(" (progress long "))
    ln_h(progressVal)
    say(string("); the cases before it are reported above"))

PRI print_pstall(progressVal) | caseIdx, repIdx
' Print the measuring cog's STALLED line, then every repetition of the case
' it stopped in that completed (its records are written).
'
' @param progressVal - the progress long: case * 16 + rep, or UNWRITTEN
'   if the cog never started a run

' Local Variables:
' @local caseIdx - case index
' @local repIdx - repetition

  ln_stall(string("measuring cog"), "P", progressVal)
  caseIdx := progressVal >> MK_CASE_SHIFT
  if progressVal <> UNWRITTEN and caseIdx < NPCASE
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_case("P", caseIdx)
    ln_s(string("repetitions completed before the stall (QX QY clocks, marker QX QY, next QX QY):"))
    if (progressVal & CUR_REP_MASK) == 0
      ln_s(string(" none"))
    else
      repeat repIdx from 0 to (progressVal & CUR_REP_MASK) - 1
        ln_s(string(" | "))
        ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_QX))
        ln_c(" ")
        ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_QY))
        ln_c(" ")
        ln_d(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_CLK))
        ln_s(string(", "))
        ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_MKX))
        ln_c(" ")
        ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_MKY))
        ln_s(string(", "))
        ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_FUX))
        ln_c(" ")
        ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_FUY))
    ln_out()

PRI print_sstall(progressVal) | caseIdx, repIdx, slotIdx
' Print the Spin2 cog's STALLED line, then every repetition of the case it
' stopped in that completed (its results are written).
'
' @param progressVal - the progress long: case * 16 + rep, or UNWRITTEN
'   if the cog never started a run

' Local Variables:
' @local caseIdx - case index
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local slotIdx - index of the repetition's results

  ln_stall(string("Spin2 cog"), "S", progressVal)
  caseIdx := progressVal >> MK_CASE_SHIFT
  if progressVal <> UNWRITTEN and caseIdx < NSCASE
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_case("S", caseIdx)
    ln_s(string("repetitions completed before the stall (result, marker, next):"))
    if (progressVal & CUR_REP_MASK) == 0
      ln_s(string(" none"))
    else
      repeat repIdx from 0 to (progressVal & CUR_REP_MASK) - 1
        slotIdx := caseIdx * REPS + repIdx
        ln_s(string(" | "))
        ln_h(spinRes[slotIdx])
        ln_c(" ")
        ln_h(spinMk[slotIdx])
        ln_c(" ")
        ln_h(spinFu[slotIdx])
    ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' tables and records
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI pcase_row(caseIdx) : pRow
' The row of a PASM case.
'
' @param caseIdx - case index
' @returns pRow - hub address of the case's pcaseTbl row

  pRow := @pcaseTbl + caseIdx * CASE_W * 4

PRI scase_row(caseIdx) : pRow
' The row of a Spin2 case.
'
' @param caseIdx - case index
' @returns pRow - hub address of the case's scaseTbl row

  pRow := @scaseTbl + caseIdx * SCASE_W * 4

PRI rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, fieldIdx) : fieldVal
' One long of a PASM case's record.
'
' @param caseIdx - case index
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @param fieldIdx - record long (RW_*)
' @returns fieldVal - that long of the case's record for the repetition

  fieldVal := precs[(caseIdx * REPS + repIdx) * RECW + fieldIdx]

PRI run_id(caseIdx, repIdx) : runId
' @param caseIdx - case index
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @returns runId - case * 16 + rep (progress long, marker, tag)

  runId := (caseIdx << MK_CASE_SHIFT) + repIdx

PRI mk_quot(caseIdx, repIdx) : quotVal
' @param caseIdx - case index
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @returns quotVal - the marker's quotient m

  quotVal := MK_BASE + run_id(caseIdx, repIdx)

PRI mk_rem(repIdx) : remVal
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @returns remVal - the marker's remainder k = (rep & 3) + 1

  remVal := (repIdx & MK_REM_MASK) + 1

PRI kind_text(kind) : pText
' @param kind - PASM form (K_*)
' @returns pText - the form as printed

  pText := lookupz(kind: string("qdiv D,#0"), string("qdiv D,S"), string("setq Q / qdiv D,#0"), string("setq Q / qdiv D,S"), string("qfrac D,#0"), string("qfrac D,S"), string("setq Q / qfrac D,#0"), string("setq Q / qfrac D,S"), string("qdiv D,#7"), string("qfrac D,#7"), string("setq Q / qdiv D,#7"), string("setq Q / qfrac D,#7"))

PRI kind_setq(kind) : bSetq
' @param kind - PASM form (K_*)
' @returns bSetq - TRUE when a SETQ Q precedes the operation

  bSetq := kind == K_DIVQ_IMM0 or kind == K_DIVQ_REG or kind == K_FRACQ_IMM0 or kind == K_FRACQ_REG or kind == K_DIVQ_IMMK or kind == K_FRACQ_IMMK

PRI kind_sreg(kind) : bSReg
' @param kind - PASM form (K_*)
' @returns bSReg - TRUE when S is a register (not an immediate)

  bSReg := kind == K_DIV_REG or kind == K_DIVQ_REG or kind == K_FRAC_REG or kind == K_FRACQ_REG

PRI op_text(opKind) : pText
' @param opKind - Spin2 operator (OP_*)
' @returns pText - the operator as printed

  pText := lookupz(opKind: string("a / b"), string("a // b"), string("a +/ b"), string("a +// b"), string("MULDIV64(a, b, c)"), string("a FRAC b"), string("a /= b"), string("a //= b"), string("a +/= b"), string("a +//= b"))

PRI op_signed(opKind) : bSigned
' @param opKind - Spin2 operator (OP_*)
' @returns bSigned - TRUE for the signed operators / and // and their
'   assignment forms

  bSigned := opKind == OP_DIV or opKind == OP_REM or opKind == OP_DIVA or opKind == OP_REMA

PRI op_gives_rem(opKind) : bRem
' @param opKind - Spin2 operator (OP_*)
' @returns bRem - TRUE for the remainder operators // and +// and their
'   assignment forms (their result comes from GETQY)

  bRem := opKind == OP_REM or opKind == OP_REMU or opKind == OP_REMA or opKind == OP_REMUA

PRI stale_of(opKind, caseIdx, repIdx, resultVal) : bStale | markerVal
' Whether a Spin2 result equals what the marker before it left in the
' CORDIC: its quotient m (GETQX operators) or its remainder k (GETQY
' operators); either sign for the signed operators.
'
' @param opKind - Spin2 operator (OP_*)
' @param caseIdx - case index
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @param resultVal - the repetition's result
' @returns bStale - TRUE when the result equals the marker's

' Local Variables:
' @local markerVal - the marker's quotient or remainder

  if op_gives_rem(opKind)
    markerVal := mk_rem(repIdx)
  else
    markerVal := mk_quot(caseIdx, repIdx)
  bStale := resultVal == markerVal or (op_signed(opKind) and resultVal == -markerVal)

PRI ln_num(numVal, bSigned)
' Append a number in hex and in signed or unsigned decimal.
'
' @param numVal - the number
' @param bSigned - TRUE: signed decimal; FALSE: unsigned

  if bSigned
    ln_hs(numVal)
  else
    ln_hu(numVal)

PRI ln_case(prefixChar, caseIdx)
' Append the case label: P07, S12.
'
' @param prefixChar - "P" or "S"
' @param caseIdx - case index

  ln_c(prefixChar)
  if caseIdx < DEC_BASE
    ln_c("0")
  ln_d(caseIdx)
  ln_c(" ")

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PASM: check and print one case
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI report_pcase(caseIdx) | pRow, kind, bCtrl, repIdx, firstX, firstY, valX, valY, sameCnt, tagCnt, mkCnt, eqMkCnt, nextCnt, ctrlCnt, clkVal, clkLo, clkHi, grpIdx
' Check one PASM case's 8 records, update the tallies and print its two
' lines and any RIG FAIL lines.
'
' @param caseIdx - case index

' Local Variables:
' @local pRow - hub address of the case's pcaseTbl row
' @local kind - the case's form (K_*)
' @local bCtrl - the case is a control
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstX - repetition 0's QX
' @local firstY - repetition 0's QY
' @local valX - the repetition's QX
' @local valY - the repetition's QY
' @local sameCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0
' @local tagCnt - records whose tag is right
' @local mkCnt - repetitions whose marker is right
' @local eqMkCnt - repetitions whose QX, QY equal the marker's
' @local nextCnt - repetitions whose NEXT divide is right
' @local ctrlCnt - repetitions equal to the control's expected values
' @local clkVal - the repetition's clocks
' @local clkLo - fewest clocks
' @local clkHi - most clocks
' @local grpIdx - clock group (G_*)

  pRow := pcase_row(caseIdx)
  kind := long[pRow][CW_KIND]
  bCtrl := caseIdx < NPCTRL
  firstX := rec_at(caseIdx, 0, RW_QX)
  firstY := rec_at(caseIdx, 0, RW_QY)
  sameCnt := 0
  tagCnt := 0
  mkCnt := 0
  eqMkCnt := 0
  nextCnt := 0
  ctrlCnt := 0
  clkLo := POSX
  clkHi := NEGX
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    valX := rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_QX)
    valY := rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_QY)
    if valX == firstX and valY == firstY
      sameCnt++
    if rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_TAG) == TAG_BASE + run_id(caseIdx, repIdx)
      tagCnt++
    if rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_MKX) == mk_quot(caseIdx, repIdx) and rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_MKY) == mk_rem(repIdx)
      mkCnt++
    if valX == rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_MKX) and valY == rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_MKY)
      eqMkCnt++
    if rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_FUX) == FU_QX and rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_FUY) == FU_QY
      nextCnt++
    if valX == long[pRow][CW_EXPX] and valY == long[pRow][CW_EXPY]
      ctrlCnt++
    clkVal := rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_CLK)
    clkLo <#= clkVal
    clkHi #>= clkVal

  ' clock group and tallies
  if bCtrl
    grpIdx := G_CTRL_PLAIN
  else
    grpIdx := G_ZERO_PLAIN
    pRunCnt += REPS
    pEqMkCnt += eqMkCnt
    pNextCnt += nextCnt
    if sameCnt == REPS
      pDetCnt++
    else
      pVarCnt++
  if kind_setq(kind)
    grpIdx++
  grpLo[grpIdx] <#= clkLo
  grpHi[grpIdx] #>= clkHi

  ' line 1: the case and its measured values
  ln_case("P", caseIdx)
  ln_s(kind_text(kind))
  ln_s(string("  D "))
  ln_hu(long[pRow][CW_D])
  if kind_sreg(kind)
    ln_s(string(" S "))
    ln_hu(long[pRow][CW_S])
  if kind_setq(kind)
    ln_s(string(" Q "))
    ln_hu(long[pRow][CW_Q])
  ln_s(string(": QX "))
  ln_hu(firstX)
  ln_s(string(" QY "))
  ln_hu(firstY)
  if sameCnt == REPS
    ln_s(string(" | DETERMINISTIC (8 of 8 identical)"))
  else
    ln_s(string(" | VARIES ("))
    ln_cnt(sameCnt)
    ln_s(string(" identical to rep 0)"))
  ln_s(string(" | equal to the marker before it "))
  ln_cnt(eqMkCnt)
  ln_s(string(" | next divide right "))
  ln_cnt(nextCnt)
  ln_s(string(" | clocks "))
  ln_d(clkLo)
  ln_s(string(".."))
  ln_d(clkHi)
  if bCtrl
    if ctrlCnt == REPS and nextCnt == REPS
      ln_s(string(" | CONTROL OK"))
    else
      ln_s(string(" | CONTROL MISS - expected QX "))
      ln_h(long[pRow][CW_EXPX])
      ln_s(string(" QY "))
      ln_h(long[pRow][CW_EXPY])
      ln_s(string(" and next divide 333 r 1, in 8 of 8"))
  ln_out()

  ' line 2: every repetition raw
  ln_s(string("  raw QX QY clocks per rep:"))
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    ln_s(string(" | "))
    ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_QX))
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_QY))
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_d(rec_at(caseIdx, repIdx, RW_CLK))
  ln_out()

  ' gates
  if bCtrl and (ctrlCnt <> REPS or nextCnt <> REPS)
    rig_fail(string("control P"))
    ln_d(caseIdx)
    ln_s(string(" right in "))
    ln_cnt(ctrlCnt)
    ln_s(string(", its next divide right in "))
    ln_cnt(nextCnt)
    ln_s(string(" (both MUST be 8 of 8)"))
    ln_out()
  if tagCnt <> REPS
    rig_fail(string("P"))
    ln_d(caseIdx)
    ln_s(string(" records with the right tag "))
    ln_cnt(tagCnt)
    ln_s(string("; rep 0 tag "))
    ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, 0, RW_TAG))
    ln_s(string(", expected "))
    ln_h(TAG_BASE + run_id(caseIdx, 0))
    ln_out()
  if mkCnt <> REPS
    rig_fail(string("P"))
    ln_d(caseIdx)
    ln_s(string(" markers right "))
    ln_cnt(mkCnt)
    ln_s(string("; rep 0 marker QX "))
    ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, 0, RW_MKX))
    ln_s(string(" QY "))
    ln_h(rec_at(caseIdx, 0, RW_MKY))
    ln_s(string(", expected "))
    ln_h(mk_quot(caseIdx, 0))
    ln_s(string(" "))
    ln_h(mk_rem(0))
    ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Spin2: the worker cog, and check and print one case
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI spin_worker() | caseIdx, repIdx, pRow, slotIdx
' Spin2 cog: run every Spin2 case 8 times, each repetition with a marker
' divide before it and the NEXT divide after it; write DONE_V at the end.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local caseIdx - Spin2 case index
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local pRow - hub address of the case's scaseTbl row
' @local slotIdx - index of the repetition's results

  repeat caseIdx from 0 to NSCASE - 1
    pRow := scase_row(caseIdx)
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      spinCur := run_id(caseIdx, repIdx)
      slotIdx := caseIdx * REPS + repIdx
      spinMk[slotIdx] := spin_op(OP_DIVU, mk_quot(caseIdx, repIdx) * MK_S + mk_rem(repIdx), MK_S, 0)
      spinRes[slotIdx] := spin_op(long[pRow][SW_OP], long[pRow][SW_A], long[pRow][SW_B], long[pRow][SW_C])
      spinFu[slotIdx] := spin_op(OP_DIVU, FU_D, FU_S, 0)
  spinDone := DONE_V

PRI spin_op(opKind, argA, argB, argC) : opResult
' One Spin2 divide.  Every operand arrives as a parameter, so the compiler
' emits the operator's bytecode and the divisor is read at run time.  The
' assignment forms load the dividend into the result, then divide it in
' place.
'
' @param opKind - Spin2 operator (OP_*)
' @param argA - the dividend; MULDIV64: the multiplier
' @param argB - the divisor; MULDIV64: the multiplicand
' @param argC - MULDIV64: the divisor (other operators: unused, 0)
' @returns opResult - the operator's result

  opResult := 0
  case opKind
    OP_DIV:
      opResult := argA / argB
    OP_REM:
      opResult := argA // argB
    OP_DIVU:
      opResult := argA +/ argB
    OP_REMU:
      opResult := argA +// argB
    OP_MD64:
      opResult := muldiv64(argA, argB, argC)
    OP_FRAC:
      opResult := argA frac argB
    OP_DIVA:
      opResult := argA
      opResult /= argB
    OP_REMA:
      opResult := argA
      opResult //= argB
    OP_DIVUA:
      opResult := argA
      opResult +/= argB
    OP_REMUA:
      opResult := argA
      opResult +//= argB

PRI report_scase(caseIdx) | pRow, opKind, bCtrl, bSigned, repIdx, slotIdx, firstVal, sameCnt, mkCnt, eqMkCnt, nextCnt, ctrlCnt
' Check one Spin2 case's 8 repetitions, update the tallies and print its two
' lines and any RIG FAIL lines.
'
' @param caseIdx - case index

' Local Variables:
' @local pRow - hub address of the case's scaseTbl row
' @local opKind - the operator (OP_*)
' @local bCtrl - the case is a control
' @local bSigned - the operator is signed
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local slotIdx - index of the repetition's results
' @local firstVal - repetition 0's result
' @local sameCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0
' @local mkCnt - repetitions whose marker is right
' @local eqMkCnt - repetitions whose result equals the marker's
' @local nextCnt - repetitions whose NEXT divide is right
' @local ctrlCnt - repetitions equal to the control's expected value

  pRow := scase_row(caseIdx)
  opKind := long[pRow][SW_OP]
  bCtrl := caseIdx < NSCTRL
  bSigned := op_signed(opKind)
  firstVal := spinRes[caseIdx * REPS]
  sameCnt := 0
  mkCnt := 0
  eqMkCnt := 0
  nextCnt := 0
  ctrlCnt := 0
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    slotIdx := caseIdx * REPS + repIdx
    if spinRes[slotIdx] == firstVal
      sameCnt++
    if spinMk[slotIdx] == mk_quot(caseIdx, repIdx)
      mkCnt++
    if stale_of(opKind, caseIdx, repIdx, spinRes[slotIdx])
      eqMkCnt++
    if spinFu[slotIdx] == FU_QX
      nextCnt++
    if spinRes[slotIdx] == long[pRow][SW_EXP]
      ctrlCnt++
  if not bCtrl
    sRunCnt += REPS
    sEqMkCnt += eqMkCnt
    sNextCnt += nextCnt
    if sameCnt == REPS
      sDetCnt++
    else
      sVarCnt++

  ' line 1: the case and its measured value
  ln_case("S", caseIdx)
  ln_s(op_text(opKind))
  ln_s(string("  a "))
  ln_num(long[pRow][SW_A], bSigned)
  ln_s(string(" b "))
  ln_num(long[pRow][SW_B], bSigned)
  if opKind == OP_MD64
    ln_s(string(" c "))
    ln_hu(long[pRow][SW_C])
  ln_s(string(": result "))
  ln_num(firstVal, bSigned)
  if sameCnt == REPS
    ln_s(string(" | DETERMINISTIC (8 of 8 identical)"))
  else
    ln_s(string(" | VARIES ("))
    ln_cnt(sameCnt)
    ln_s(string(" identical to rep 0)"))
  ln_s(string(" | equal to the marker before it "))
  ln_cnt(eqMkCnt)
  ln_s(string(" | next divide right "))
  ln_cnt(nextCnt)
  if bCtrl
    if ctrlCnt == REPS and nextCnt == REPS
      ln_s(string(" | CONTROL OK"))
    else
      ln_s(string(" | CONTROL MISS - expected "))
      ln_num(long[pRow][SW_EXP], bSigned)
      ln_s(string(" and next divide 333, in 8 of 8"))
  ln_out()

  ' line 2: every repetition raw
  ln_s(string("  raw result per rep:"))
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_h(spinRes[caseIdx * REPS + repIdx])
  ln_out()

  ' gates
  if bCtrl and (ctrlCnt <> REPS or nextCnt <> REPS)
    rig_fail(string("control S"))
    ln_d(caseIdx)
    ln_s(string(" right in "))
    ln_cnt(ctrlCnt)
    ln_s(string(", its next divide right in "))
    ln_cnt(nextCnt)
    ln_s(string(" (both MUST be 8 of 8)"))
    ln_out()
  if mkCnt <> REPS
    rig_fail(string("S"))
    ln_d(caseIdx)
    ln_s(string(" markers right "))
    ln_cnt(mkCnt)
    ln_s(string("; rep 0 marker "))
    ln_h(spinMk[caseIdx * REPS])
    ln_s(string(", expected "))
    ln_h(mk_quot(caseIdx, 0))
    ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' summary
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_grp(grpIdx)
' Append a clock group's range "lo..hi" (or "none").
'
' @param grpIdx - clock group (G_*)

  if grpLo[grpIdx] > grpHi[grpIdx]
    ln_s(string("none"))
  else
    ln_d(grpLo[grpIdx])
    ln_s(string(".."))
    ln_d(grpHi[grpIdx])

PRI print_summary()
' Print the SUMMARY, CONTROLS and END lines.
'

  say(string("=== SUMMARY ==="))
  ln_s(string("SUMMARY PASM: zero-divisor cases DETERMINISTIC "))
  ln_d(pDetCnt)
  ln_s(string(", VARIES "))
  ln_d(pVarCnt)
  ln_s(string(" (of "))
  ln_d(pRanCnt - NPCTRL #> 0)
  ln_s(string(" run); equal to the marker before them in "))
  ln_d(pEqMkCnt)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(pRunCnt)
  ln_s(string(" runs; next divide right after "))
  ln_d(pNextCnt)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(pRunCnt)
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("SUMMARY PASM clocks, GETCT before the op to GETCT after its GETQX: no SETQ - controls "))
  ln_grp(G_CTRL_PLAIN)
  ln_s(string(", zero divisor "))
  ln_grp(G_ZERO_PLAIN)
  ln_s(string("; with SETQ - controls "))
  ln_grp(G_CTRL_SETQ)
  ln_s(string(", zero divisor "))
  ln_grp(G_ZERO_SETQ)
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("SUMMARY SPIN2: zero-divisor cases DETERMINISTIC "))
  ln_d(sDetCnt)
  ln_s(string(", VARIES "))
  ln_d(sVarCnt)
  ln_s(string(" (of "))
  ln_d(sRanCnt - NSCTRL #> 0)
  ln_s(string(" run); equal to the marker before them in "))
  ln_d(sEqMkCnt)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(sRunCnt)
  ln_s(string(" runs; next divide right after "))
  ln_d(sNextCnt)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(sRunCnt)
  ln_out()
  if failCnt == 0 and pRanCnt > NPCTRL and sRanCnt > NSCTRL
    say(string("CONTROLS: OK - every control exact in 8 of 8 with its next divide, every marker right, every record tag right"))
  else
    ln_s(string("CONTROLS: RIG FAIL - "))
    ln_d(failCnt)
    say(string(" RIG FAIL line(s) above, or a cog stalled before its controls ran; the values above are raw, not results"))
  if bPasmStall or bSpinStall
    say(string("=== END: STALLED (see the STALLED line) ==="))
  elseif failCnt == 0
    say(string("=== END: CONTROLS OK ==="))
  else
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL ==="))

DAT ' ---- PASM Cases: form, D, S, Q, expected QX, expected QY ----
' controls P00..P10 (non-zero divisors; the expected values MUST appear)
pcaseTbl        long    K_DIV_REG,    1000,       3,          0,          333,        1
                long    K_DIV_REG,    $FFFF_FFFF, 2,          0,          $7FFF_FFFF, 1
                long    K_DIV_REG,    0,          5,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_REG,    7,          $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0,          7
                long    K_DIV_IMMK,   $1234_5678, CTL_IMM_S,  0,          $0299_C335, 5
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   $9ABC_DEF0, $8765_4321, $1234_5678, $226B_9022, $38BC_648E
                long    K_FRAC_REG,   1,          3,          0,          $5555_5555, 1
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  1,          7,          $8000_0000, $36DB_6DB6, 6
                long    K_FRAC_IMMK,  1,          CTL_IMM_S,  0,          $2492_4924, 4
                long    K_DIVQ_IMMK,  $1234_5678, CTL_IMM_S,  3,          $7050_9EA3, 3
                long    K_FRACQ_IMMK, 2,          CTL_IMM_S,  $1234_5678, $4BBE_557E, 6
' zero divisor P11..P60 (S = #0, or S = a register holding 0)
pzeroTbl        long    K_DIV_IMM0,   0,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_REG,    0,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_IMM0,   1,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_REG,    1,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_IMM0,   7,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_REG,    7,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_IMM0,   $7FFF_FFFF, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_REG,    $7FFF_FFFF, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_IMM0,   $8000_0000, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_REG,    $8000_0000, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_IMM0,   $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_REG,    $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_IMM0,   $1234_5678, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIV_REG,    $1234_5678, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   0,          0,          1,          0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   7,          0,          1,          0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          1,          0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_IMM0,  7,          0,          1,          0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   0,          0,          $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   7,          0,          $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_IMM0,  7,          0,          $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   0,          0,          $1234_5678, 0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   7,          0,          $1234_5678, 0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_REG,   $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          $1234_5678, 0,          0
                long    K_DIVQ_IMM0,  7,          0,          $1234_5678, 0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_IMM0,  0,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_REG,   0,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_IMM0,  1,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_REG,   1,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_IMM0,  7,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_REG,   7,          0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_IMM0,  $8000_0000, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_REG,   $8000_0000, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_IMM0,  $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_REG,   $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_IMM0,  $1234_5678, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRAC_REG,   $1234_5678, 0,          0,          0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  0,          0,          1,          0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  1,          0,          1,          0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  $1234_5678, 0,          1,          0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_IMM0, 1,          0,          1,          0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  0,          0,          $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  1,          0,          $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  $1234_5678, 0,          $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_IMM0, 1,          0,          $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  0,          0,          $1234_5678, 0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  1,          0,          $1234_5678, 0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_REG,  $1234_5678, 0,          $1234_5678, 0,          0
                long    K_FRACQ_IMM0, 1,          0,          $1234_5678, 0,          0
pcaseEnd

DAT ' ---- Spin2 Cases: operator, a, b, c, expected ----
' controls S00..S20 (non-zero divisors; the expected value MUST appear)
scaseTbl        long    OP_DIV,  1000,        3,          0,          333
                long    OP_DIV,  -1000,       3,          0,          -333
                long    OP_DIV,  1000,        -3,         0,          -333
                long    OP_DIV,  -1000,       -3,         0,          333
                long    OP_REM,  1000,        3,          0,          1
                long    OP_REM,  -1000,       3,          0,          -1
                long    OP_REM,  1000,        -3,         0,          1
                long    OP_REM,  -1000,       -3,         0,          -1
                long    OP_DIVU, $FFFF_FFFF,  2,          0,          $7FFF_FFFF
                long    OP_DIVU, 1000,        3,          0,          333
                long    OP_REMU, $FFFF_FFFF,  2,          0,          1
                long    OP_REMU, 1000,        7,          0,          6
                long    OP_MD64, 1000,        1000,       3,          333333
                long    OP_MD64, $FFFF_FFFF,  $FFFF_FFFF, $FFFF_FFFF, $FFFF_FFFF
                long    OP_MD64, $1234_5678,  $10,        3,          $6117_2280
                long    OP_FRAC, 1,           3,          0,          $5555_5555
                long    OP_FRAC, 2,           7,          0,          $4924_9249
                long    OP_DIVA, -1000,       3,          0,          -333
                long    OP_REMA, -1000,       3,          0,          -1
                long    OP_DIVUA, $FFFF_FFFF, 2,          0,          $7FFF_FFFF
                long    OP_REMUA, 1000,       7,          0,          6
' zero divisor S21..S70 (b = 0; MULDIV64: c = 0)
szeroTbl        long    OP_DIV,  0,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIV,  1,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIV,  7,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIV,  -1,          0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIV,  -7,          0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIV,  $7FFF_FFFF,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIV,  NEGX,        0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIV,  $1234_5678,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIV,  -$1234_5678, 0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REM,  0,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REM,  1,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REM,  7,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REM,  -1,          0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REM,  -7,          0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REM,  $7FFF_FFFF,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REM,  NEGX,        0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REM,  $1234_5678,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REM,  -$1234_5678, 0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIVU, 0,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIVU, 1,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIVU, 7,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIVU, $7FFF_FFFF,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIVU, $8000_0000,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIVU, $FFFF_FFFF,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIVU, $1234_5678,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REMU, 0,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REMU, 1,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REMU, 7,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REMU, $7FFF_FFFF,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REMU, $8000_0000,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REMU, $FFFF_FFFF,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REMU, $1234_5678,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_MD64, 0,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_MD64, 0,           12345,      0,          0
                long    OP_MD64, 1,           1,          0,          0
                long    OP_MD64, 7,           3,          0,          0
                long    OP_MD64, 1000,        1000,       0,          0
                long    OP_MD64, $1234_5678,  $10,        0,          0
                long    OP_MD64, $FFFF_FFFF,  $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0
                long    OP_MD64, $1234_5678,  $9ABC_DEF0, 0,          0
                long    OP_FRAC, 0,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_FRAC, 1,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_FRAC, 7,           0,          0,          0
                long    OP_FRAC, $8000_0000,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_FRAC, $FFFF_FFFF,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_FRAC, $1234_5678,  0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIVA, -7,          0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REMA, -7,          0,          0,          0
                long    OP_DIVUA, $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0,          0
                long    OP_REMUA, $FFFF_FFFF, 0,          0,          0
scaseEnd

' ===========================================================================
' MEASURING COG (PASM, cog exec).  PTRA on entry = @mbox (from COGINIT).
' No debug(), no BRK, no interrupt in this cog (DEBUG_COGS excludes it).
' Every CORDIC result is read with GETQX / GETQY before the next CORDIC
' operation is issued, so at most one result is ever in flight.
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Cog ----
pasm            rdlong  c_tbl, ptra[MB_TBL]             ' hub address of pcaseTbl
                rdlong  c_rp, ptra[MB_REC]              ' hub address of the records
                rdlong  c_ncase, ptra[MB_NCASE]
                mov     c_case, #0

case_lp         rdlong  c_kind, c_tbl                   ' the case row: form, D, S, Q
                add     c_tbl, #4
                rdlong  dval, c_tbl
                add     c_tbl, #4
                rdlong  sval, c_tbl
                add     c_tbl, #4
                rdlong  qval, c_tbl
                add     c_tbl, #(CASE_W - CW_Q) * 4     ' to the next row
                alts    c_kind, #kvec_tab
                mov     c_vec, 0-0                      ' the form's code
                mov     c_rep, #0

rep_lp          mov     r_tag, c_case                   ' case * 16 + rep
                shl     r_tag, #MK_CASE_SHIFT
                add     r_tag, c_rep
                wrlong  r_tag, ptra[MB_CUR]             ' progress: the run about to start
                mov     c_mkq, r_tag
                add     c_mkq, c_mkbase                 ' marker quotient m
                mov     c_mkd, c_mkq
                shl     c_mkd, #3
                sub     c_mkd, c_mkq                    ' 7 * m
                mov     c_mkr, c_rep
                and     c_mkr, #MK_REM_MASK
                add     c_mkr, #1                       ' marker remainder k = (rep & 3) + 1
                add     c_mkd, c_mkr                    ' marker numerator 7 * m + k
                qdiv    c_mkd, c_mks                    ' MARKER: a non-zero divide
                getqx   r_mkx
                getqy   r_mky
                jmp     c_vec                           ' THE CASE (one copy per form)

case_done       mov     r_clk, c_t1
                sub     r_clk, c_t0                     ' GETCT to GETCT
                qdiv    c_fud, c_fus                    ' NEXT: 1000 / 3
                getqx   r_fux
                getqy   r_fuy
                add     r_tag, c_tagbase
                setq    #RECW - 1
                wrlong  r_mkx, c_rp                     ' the record, 8 longs, tag last
                add     c_rp, #RECW * 4
                add     c_rep, #1
                cmp     c_rep, #REPS                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #rep_lp
                add     c_case, #1
                cmp     c_case, c_ncase                 wz
        if_nz   jmp     #case_lp
                wrlong  c_donev, ptra[MB_DONE]
                cogid   c_t0
                cogstop c_t0

'--- the forms, one hand-written copy each (kvec_tab order = K_* order)
f_div_imm0      getct   c_t0
                qdiv    dval, #0                        ' D / #0
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_div_reg       getct   c_t0
                qdiv    dval, sval                      ' D / S
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_divq_imm0     getct   c_t0
                setq    qval
                qdiv    dval, #0                        ' {Q:D} / #0
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_divq_reg      getct   c_t0
                setq    qval
                qdiv    dval, sval                      ' {Q:D} / S
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_frac_imm0     getct   c_t0
                qfrac   dval, #0                        ' {D:0} / #0
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_frac_reg      getct   c_t0
                qfrac   dval, sval                      ' {D:0} / S
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_fracq_imm0    getct   c_t0
                setq    qval
                qfrac   dval, #0                        ' {D:Q} / #0
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_fracq_reg     getct   c_t0
                setq    qval
                qfrac   dval, sval                      ' {D:Q} / S
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_div_immk      getct   c_t0
                qdiv    dval, #CTL_IMM_S                ' D / #7 (control P04)
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_frac_immk     getct   c_t0
                qfrac   dval, #CTL_IMM_S                ' {D:0} / #7 (control P08)
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_divq_immk     getct   c_t0
                setq    qval
                qdiv    dval, #CTL_IMM_S                ' {Q:D} / #7 (control P09)
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

f_fracq_immk    getct   c_t0
                setq    qval
                qfrac   dval, #CTL_IMM_S                ' {D:Q} / #7 (control P10)
                getqx   r_qx
                getct   c_t1
                getqy   r_qy
                jmp     #case_done

'--- form vectors
kvec_tab        long    f_div_imm0, f_div_reg, f_divq_imm0, f_divq_reg, f_frac_imm0, f_frac_reg, f_fracq_imm0, f_fracq_reg
                long    f_div_immk, f_frac_immk, f_divq_immk, f_fracq_immk

'--- cog data
c_mkbase        long    MK_BASE
c_mks           long    MK_S                            ' marker divisor (register S)
c_fud           long    FU_D                            ' NEXT divide: 1000 / 3
c_fus           long    FU_S
c_tagbase       long    TAG_BASE
c_donev         long    DONE_V
dval            long    0                               ' the case's D
sval            long    0                               ' the case's S (register forms)
qval            long    0                               ' the case's Q (SETQ forms)
c_tbl           long    0
c_rp            long    0
c_ncase         long    0
c_case          long    0
c_rep           long    0
c_kind          long    0
c_vec           long    0
c_mkq           long    0
c_mkd           long    0
c_mkr           long    0
c_t0            long    0
c_t1            long    0
'--- the record, written as one 8-long block in this order (RW_* order)
r_mkx           long    0                               ' marker QX
r_mky           long    0                               ' marker QY
r_qx            long    0                               ' the case's QX
r_qy            long    0                               ' the case's QY
r_clk           long    0                               ' GETCT to GETCT
r_fux           long    0                               ' NEXT QX
r_fuy           long    0                               ' NEXT QY
r_tag           long    0                               ' TAG_BASE + case * 16 + rep
pasm_end

